,\" don't partition.\"]}],\" A listing whose floor the source never stated is in neither.\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",\"li-3\",{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",\"strong-0\",{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"code\",\"code-0\",{\"dir\":\"ltr\",\"children\":\"verified=false\"}],\" means \\\"not marked verified\\\"\"]}],\", which includes every listing the source said nothing about — not only ones it marked unverified.\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",\"li-4\",{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",\"strong-0\",{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"code\",\"code-0\",{\"dir\":\"ltr\",\"children\":\"neighborhood_id_exclude\"}],\" keeps listings Kite couldn't place\"]}],\"; \",[\"$\",\"code\",\"code-0\",{\"dir\":\"ltr\",\"children\":\"neighborhood_id\"}],\" drops them. Excluding three neighborhoods is therefore not the same as including all the others.\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",\"li-5\",{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",\"strong-0\",{\"children\":[\"A misspelled \",[\"$\",\"code\",\"code-0\",{\"dir\":\"ltr\",\"children\":\"source\"}],\" narrows to nothing.\"]}],\" Parameter \",[\"$\",\"em\",\"em-0\",{\"children\":\"names\"}],\" are validated, so a typo there is an \",[\"$\",\"code\",\"code-0\",{\"dir\":\"ltr\",\"children\":\"unknown_parameter\"}],\" error — but source values aren't checked against the list, so \",[\"$\",\"code\",\"code-1\",{\"dir\":\"ltr\",\"children\":\"source=bayutt\"}],\" quietly returns an empty page. \",[\"$\",\"code\",\"code-2\",{\"dir\":\"ltr\",\"children\":\"GET /enums\"}],\" has the real ones.\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",\"li-6\",{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",\"strong-0\",{\"children\":\"Listings with no price never appear in search\"}],\", even though \",[\"$\",\"code\",\"code-0\",{\"dir\":\"ltr\",\"children\":\"price.yearly_sar\"}],\" is nullable and a detail lookup can return one.\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",\"li-7\",{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",\"strong-0\",{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"code\",\"code-0\",{\"dir\":\"ltr\",\"children\":\"property_type\"}],\" with several values shifts the quality bounds.\"]}],\" The outlier filter calibrates per property type only when you ask for exactly one, so a villa excluded by \",[\"$\",\"code\",\"code-0\",{\"dir\":\"ltr\",\"children\":\"property_type=villa\"}],\" can appear under \",[\"$\",\"code\",\"code-1\",{\"dir\":\"ltr\",\"children\":\"property_type=villa,apartment\"}],\".\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",\"li-8\",{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",\"strong-0\",{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"code\",\"code-0\",{\"dir\":\"ltr\",\"children\":\"sort=price_drop\"}],\" also filters\"]}],\", to listings whose price actually fell. And \",[\"$\",\"code\",\"code-0\",{\"dir\":\"ltr\",\"children\":\"sort=recommended\"}],\" is a ranking that gets retuned between releases, so the same query can reorder — page through it freely, but don't sync with it.\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",\"li-9\",{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",\"strong-0\",{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"code\",\"code-0\",{\"dir\":\"ltr\",\"children\":\"compound=true\"}],\" is a special case\"]}],\" meaning \\\"in any compound\\\", not a compound named \\\"true\\\". Use \",[\"$\",\"code\",\"code-0\",{\"dir\":\"ltr\",\"children\":\"in_compound\"}],\" if that's what you meant.\"]}],\"\\n\"]}]\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"66:[\"$\",\"h2\",\"h2-1\",{\"id\":\"counts-won-t-match-darak-app-exactly\",\"className\":\"scroll-mt-20\",\"children\":\"Counts won't match kite.sa exactly\"}]\n67:[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-3\",{\"children\":\"Both now serve all live inventory, so the two should agree closely. Where they differ it's the ranking and the outlier filter, not a freshness window — kite.sa used to hide listings whose source hadn't restated an update date in 30 days, which turned out to exclude a fifth of live listings and to depend almost entirely on which source published them. That filter is gone.\"}]\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"35:C\n31:C\n34:C\n2a:C\n27:C\n1f:C\n1c:C\n17:C\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"69:\"SearchSiteHeader\"\n6a:I[119537,[\"$6